From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MLD STA: take a Beacon protection failure on any link

wpas_event_unprot_beacon() compared the SA of the Beacon frame with
wpa_s->bssid. With the SME in user space, that is the AP MLD address,
while mac80211 does not translate the address of a Beacon frame, so an
MLD station ignored each Beacon protection failure. With the SME in the
driver, wpa_s->bssid is the BSSID of the association link, so a failure
on another link was ignored. Look the SA up in the links.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/wpa_supplicant/events.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/events.c
@@ -6599,16 +6599,19 @@ static void wpas_event_unprot_beacon(str
 				     struct unprot_beacon *data)
 {
 	struct wpabuf *buf;
-	int res, freq;
+	int res, freq, link_id;
 
-	if (!data || wpa_s->wpa_state != WPA_COMPLETED ||
+	if (!data || wpa_s->wpa_state != WPA_COMPLETED)
+		return;
+
+	link_id = wpas_ap_link_id_by_bssid(wpa_s, data->sa);
+	if (wpa_s->valid_links ? link_id < 0 :
 	    !ether_addr_equal(data->sa, wpa_s->bssid))
 		return;
 	wpa_msg(wpa_s, MSG_INFO, WPA_EVENT_UNPROT_BEACON MACSTR,
 		MAC2STR(data->sa));
 
-	freq = wpas_ap_link_freq(wpa_s,
-				 wpas_ap_link_id_by_bssid(wpa_s, data->sa));
+	freq = wpas_ap_link_freq(wpa_s, link_id);
 	if (freq < 0) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
 			   "Link of the Beacon frame has no channel for the WNM-Notification Request frame");
